<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 1.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 1.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to March 1 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Feb 23-March 1</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,939,543 tns	218,078 tns    11.24 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,923,642 tns	216,110 tns    11.23 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,652,261 tns	188,219 tns    11.39 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to March 1</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    20,140,734 tns    2,130,752 tns    10.58 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    19,402,704 tns    2,012,384 tns    10.37 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    18,387,520 tns    1,899,202 tns    10.33 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 60 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 59 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 58 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
